  "content": {
    "id": "p76-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "40 animals are released on an island with carrying capacity 1000. The population $N$ satisfies:\n$$\\frac{dN}{dt}=kN(1000-N),$$\nfor some constant $k$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p76-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\displaystyle\\frac{1000}{N(1000-N)}=\\frac1N+\\frac1{1000-N}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\frac1N+\\frac1{1000-N}=\\frac{1000-N+N}{N(1000-N)}=\\frac{1000}{N(1000-N)}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1N+\\frac1{1000-N}&=\\frac{1000-N+N}{N(1000-N)}\\\\&=\\frac{1000}{N(1000-N)}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p76-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Use part a to find the general solution.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle N=\\frac{1000}{1+Be^{-1000kt}}$, where $B$ is an arbitrary constant. Also $N=0$ is a constant solution.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dN}{N(1000-N)}&=k\\,dt\\\\\\frac1{1000}\\left(\\frac1N+\\frac1{1000-N}\\right)dN&=k\\,dt.\\end{align*}$$\nIntegrate:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{1000}\\bigl(\\ln|N|-\\ln|1000-N|\\bigr)&=kt+C\\\\\\ln\\left|\\frac{N}{1000-N}\\right|&=1000kt+C_1\\\\\\frac{N}{1000-N}&=Ae^{1000kt}.\\end{align*}$$\nRearranging:\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=1000Ae^{1000kt}-NAe^{1000kt}\\\\N(1+Ae^{1000kt})&=1000Ae^{1000kt}\\\\N&=\\frac{1000}{1+Be^{-1000kt}},\\end{align*}$$\nwhere $B=\\frac{1}{A}$. The constant solutions are $N=0$ and $N=1000$; the latter is included by taking $B=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p76-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Determine the arbitrary constant using $N(0)=40$, then simplify.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$B=24$; $\\displaystyle N=\\frac{1000}{1+24e^{-1000kt}}$.",
          "worked": "Using $N(0)=40$:\n$$\\begin{align*}40&=\\frac{1000}{1+B}\\\\1+B&=25\\\\B&=24\\\\N&=\\frac{1000}{1+24e^{-1000kt}}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      },
      {
        "id": "p76-q14-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Given the population after 1 year was 80, find $k$ correct to four significant figures.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k\\approx7.357\\times10^{-4}$.",
          "worked": "Using $N(1)=80$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1000}{1+24e^{-1000k}}&=80\\\\1+24e^{-1000k}&=12.5\\\\e^{-1000k}&=\\frac{11.5}{24}\\\\-1000k&=\\ln\\left(\\frac{11.5}{24}\\right)\\\\k&=-\\frac1{1000}\\ln\\left(\\frac{11.5}{24}\\right)\\\\&\\approx7.357\\times10^{-4}\\quad\\text{(4 significant figures).}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p76-q14-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "What will the population be after 5 years, to the nearest whole number?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "623 animals.",
          "worked": "Using the unrounded value of $k$:\n$$\\begin{align*}N(5)&=\\frac{1000}{1+24e^{-5000k}}\\\\&=\\frac{1000}{1+24\\left(\\frac{11.5}{24}\\right)^5}\\\\&\\approx623.\\end{align*}$$\nThe population will be approximately 623 animals.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      }
    ]
  },
